      8   2   0.000   0.220   0.220   0.772     6
      8   4   0.024   0.167   0.270   0.714     6

  'deg1' is the fraction of the indicator expressible at degree 1, which is
  all the shipped drift has. 'cap@1' is n+1, the enhancement ceiling there.
  Physical landscapes concentrating indicator weight at LOW degree, well
  above the random control, is the structure a low-degree drift could
  exploit - and the size of that gap is the size of the opportunity. If
  the physical rows match the random rows, then these landscapes are
  unstructured from the drift's point of view and no low-degree phase
  helps, whatever the mixer.
